+/* gdx-3 (#984) — Technique T1 on .pref-dot: the player-facing rating dot the
+   issue was reaching for when it named `.dot` (which is ST-editor-only and
+   stays carved out).
+   The box is genuinely invisible - no background, border, shadow or radius, and
+   .filled only recolours the 30px glyph - so growing it to --tap-min shows
+   nothing new in itself. What WOULD show is the knock-on: six more pixels per
+   dot would spread the glyph pitch and six more would move the row's separator
+   rule. The negative margin gives those six pixels back to the layout, so the
+   dot OCCUPIES the 38px it always did (pitch 46px, run 222px, row 66px, all
+   unchanged) while its hit area is a true 44 by 44. Adjacent hit areas end up
+   2px apart, so nothing overlaps, which is AC2.
+   Written as a calc off the token rather than a bare -3px so the compensation
