public/css/suite.css-80-/* Phone bottom nav (issue #596): +25% size, safe-area-inset reservation, and an
public/css/suite.css-81- * edge-gradient scroll affordance. Affordance is pure CSS (mask-image, option b
public/css/suite.css-82- * in the issue) — no JS, no z-index/pointer-events trap on the nav buttons. The
public/css/suite.css-83- * fade is phone-scoped (≤599px) so the ≥600px flex-start layout doesn't get a
public/css/suite.css-84- * cosmetic fade over its empty right gutter. Safe-area uses the .cr-box pattern
public/css/suite.css-85- * at line 683; on desktop the inset evaluates to 0 so only the 8px buffer adds. */
public/css/suite.css:86:#bnav{flex-shrink:0;display:flex;background:var(--surf2);border-top:1px solid var(--bdr);z-index:20;position:relative;overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;scrollbar-width:none;padding:0 2px calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));overscroll-behavior-x:contain;touch-action:pan-x;}
