-  - **Triggering input or sequence:** At a viewport of 600px or wider, render the diff's own real-chain fixture, `.sheet-topbar > .svt-toggle > .svt-btn`, and tap above or below the button's roughly 24px visible box. The broad T2 selector `.sheet-topbar button::after` also matches `.svt-btn`, even though the T3 rationale says `.svt-btn` cannot use an overlay because `.svt-toggle` clips it with `overflow:hidden`. The T3 `min-height` is limited to `max-width:599px`.
-  - **Observable consequence:** On desktop, the nominal 44px pseudo-element is clipped to the small segmented-control box and the visible box is deliberately asserted to remain 24px high. Users therefore do not get the claimed 44px effective target. The 360px test passes via T3 box growth, while the desktop unchanged-size test measures only the border box and never verifies tappability; the desktop sidebar test is unrelated.
-  - **Confidence:** High. This follows directly from selector matching, the diff's explicit clipping statement, the media-query boundary, and the supplied fixtures/tests.
+### [Pass 1] An unrelated selector rewrite removes the downtime radio/checkbox text-colour rule
+
+- **Severity**: Medium
+- **File:line**: `public/css/suite.css:1702`
+- **Triggering input or sequence**: Render any downtime quick-form radio label, or a checkbox label under the normal single `#t-downtime` container. The diff removes the grouped `.qf-radio-label, .qf-checkbox-label` rule and replaces it with `#t-downtime #t-downtime .qf-checkbox-label`.
+- **Observable consequence**: The radio label no longer receives this scoped `color: var(--txt)` declaration at all. The checkbox declaration now requires one `#t-downtime` beneath another identically-ID'd ancestor, so it does not match the normal DOM either. Both controls can inherit a different colour, creating an unrelated visible regression outside the touch-target work.
+- **Confidence**: High. This follows directly from selector matching; runtime confirmation is deferred to Pass 2 because Pass 1 may inspect only the diff.
 
