public/css/suite.css-2736-   FOUR TRAPS, all real in this tree, all handled below:
public/css/suite.css:2737:   1. overflow:hidden on an ancestor clips the overlay. .svt-toggle has it, so
public/css/suite.css-2738-      .svt-btn takes T3. .hdr-char-menu-item has its own, so it takes T3 too.
public/css/suite.css:2739:   2. .tab{overflow-x:hidden} clips horizontal expansion at the tab edge. .tab is
public/css/suite.css-2740-      position:absolute;inset:0, so vertical expansion is unaffected.
public/css/suite.css-2741-   3. the element must not already own the pseudo-element. Two do:
public/css/suite.css-2742-      .hdr-icon-wrap.has-menu (its chevron badge) and .status-summary--toggle
--
public/css/suite.css-2924-            neighbour is another tracker box. A mis-tap would mark the wrong
public/css/suite.css-2925-            point of damage, which is worse than the small target. The box grows
public/css/suite.css-2926-            instead, so the run stays collision-free.
public/css/suite.css:2927:   .svt-btn parent .svt-toggle is overflow:hidden (it clips the segmented
public/css/suite.css-2928-            control's 4px corner radius), which clips any overlay - trap 1.
public/css/suite.css-2929-            The parent is left alone so the corners still clip.
public/css/suite.css:2930:   .hdr-char-menu-item carries its OWN overflow:hidden (for the name ellipsis),
public/css/suite.css-2931-            so its overlay is clipped to its own box - trap 1 again.
public/css/suite.css-2932-   the six <select> controls - Chromium generates no pseudo-element box on a
public/css/suite.css-2933-            form control at all, so T2 is inert on them (see the note above the
