1: # Story gdx.3: 44px effective hit areas on the player game-night surfaces
2: 
3: Status: review
4: 
5: ## Story
6: 
7: As a player (or an ST) using the app on a phone at a live game,
8: I want every control I have to tap to have a finger-sized hit area,
9: so that I can spend Vitae, mark damage, flip a toggle or pick a modifier in a dim room without
10: mis-tapping the control next to the one I meant.
11: 
12: ## Why this story exists
13: 
14: GitHub issue #984, Epic GDX Group A (mobile hygiene, independent of Groups B and C). The issue's own
15: wording is short:
16: 
17: > Pad hit areas (not visual size) to >=44px: tappable rating dots (`components.css:48`, 18px today),
18: > `.edit-tab` strip (`components.css:174`, ~30px), `.svt-btn` toggles (`suite.css:730`, ~26px),
19: > tracker tap zones.
20: > AC: (1) All interactive player-surface controls have >=44px hit areas. (2) Desktop visual design
21: > unchanged.
22: 
23: 44px is the WCAG 2.5.5 (Target Size, AAA) figure and the number this repo has already standardised on
24: in five earlier stories (see "Existing convention" in Dev Notes). It is not a new introduction here.
25: 
26: ## Measured baseline (verified during story creation, 2026-08-20)
27: 
28: Every figure and line reference below was re-derived from the current tree. **Do not trust issue
29: #984's own numbers** without checking; one of its four is stale and one of its four points at the
30: wrong element. gdx-2 hit the same problem with issue #983.
31: 
32: **Audit method.** Every rule in `public/css/suite.css` and `public/css/components.css` carrying
33: `cursor:pointer` was extracted and its box height derived from `height` / `min-height`, or from
34: `padding` plus `line-height` (falling back to `font-size` x 1.2). Result:
35: 
36: | Bucket | Count |
37: |---|---|
38: | `cursor:pointer` rules, both files | **218** |
39: | already >= 44px | 24 |
40: | below 44px (derived) | 140 |
41: | not statically derivable (no height, no padding, or content-sized) | 54 |
42: 
43: Each selector was then mapped to the JS module or HTML file that emits it, so player surfaces could
44: be separated from ST-only ones. `public/js/app.js`'s `NAV_ITEMS` and `MORE_APPS` carry the
45: `stOnly` / `coordinatorOnly` flags that decide this; the ST-only tabs are `territory`,
46: `office-approvals`, `tracker`, `combat`, `spheres`, `signin` and `emergency`.
47: 
48: ### The issue's four named targets, as they actually are
49: 
50: | Issue says | Reality | Verdict |
51: |---|---|---|
52: | "tappable rating dots (`components.css:48`, 18px today)" | `.dot{width:18px;height:18px}` is at **`components.css:48`** and is **18px** - both correct. But `.dot` is emitted **only** by `public/js/editor/attrs-tab.js` (the ST character editor's Attributes and Skills panes). A player never renders it. The genuinely player-facing tappable rating dot is **`.pref-dot`** (`components.css:6081`, **38x38**), the Chronicle Preferences stepper on the Ordeals/XP tab, emitted by `public/js/tabs/ordeals-view.js:125`. | `.dot` **carved out** (see the scoping call below). `.pref-dot` **in scope** - it is the control the bullet was reaching for. |
53: | "`.edit-tab` strip (`components.css:174`, ~30px)" | `.edit-tab{padding:8px 14px;font-size:0.625rem}` is at **`components.css:174`**. Derived height **28px** (8 + 8 + a ~12px line box at 10px). Width is already comfortable (roughly 108px for "ATTRIBUTES"), so this is a **height-only** problem. | **In scope.** See the scoping call. |
54: | "`.svt-btn` toggles (`suite.css:730`, ~26px)" | Real line is **`suite.css:750`**, not 730. Derived height **23.2px** (`padding:5px 12px`, `font-size:var(--fs-floor-micro)` = 11px). Note the font-size is a `var()` because gdx-2 raised it from a literal 10px; before gdx-2 this rule derived to 22.4px. | **In scope.** |
55: | "tracker tap zones" | Unspecified in the issue. Resolves to **two different things**: (a) the **player's** tracker, `.tbox` (`suite.css:243`, **34x30**), the health/vitae/willpower/influence boxes on the sheet, emitted by `public/js/suite/sheet.js:148/403/888`, plus `.sh-tracker-info-btn` (`suite.css:2269`, **16x16**); and (b) the **ST Tracker tab** (`#t-tracker`, `stOnly:true`), whose `.trk-adj` is **28x28** and `.trk-adj.sm` **24x24** (`suite.css:640-641`). | **Both in scope.** (a) is player-facing. (b) is ST-only but the issue names it by name and it is the ST's most-tapped screen at a live game; it costs one rule. |
56: 
57: ## Scoping call on `.edit-tab` (read gdx-2's precedent before this section makes sense)
58: 
59: gdx-2 raised the same question and Angelus ruled on it. From
60: `specs/stories/gdx-2-mobile-type-scale.md`'s Review Findings section:
61: 
62: > **Resolved by Angelus 2026-08-20 ... `.edit-tab`/`.edit-dirty` stay unraised - they are ST-only
63: > tooling chrome a player never sees, not player content, so AC2's floor doesn't need to reach them.**
64: 
65: That ruling is about a **text-size floor**. It was re-examined here rather than inherited, because
66: touch targets are a different concern, and the re-examination reaches a **different conclusion for
67: `.edit-tab` and the same conclusion for `.dot`**. The reasoning, explicitly:
68: 
69: **Why gdx-2's logic does not transfer to `.edit-tab`.**
70: 1. gdx-2's ruling turned on *cost versus benefit for legibility*: an ST does not need a 10px tab
71:    label enlarged, and enlarging it would cost editor density. Touch targets have a different
72:    benefit profile. `public/index.html` hosts the full ST editor (`editorRenderSheet` is called into
73:    it whenever `getRole()==='st'`, established as fact by gdx-2's own Acceptance Auditor layer), so
74:    an ST editing a sheet from their phone mid-session really does tap `.edit-tab`. It is the **only**
75:    control that moves between editor panes, so a missed tap is a hard block, not a comfort issue.
76: 2. The objection that decided gdx-2 does not exist here. gdx-2's change was visible; this story's is
77:    not. `.edit-tab` takes **Technique T2** (a transparent hit-area pseudo-element, see Dev Notes), so
78:    the admin editor renders pixel-identically before and after. The density argument has nothing to
79:    bite on.
80: 3. It is geometrically clean. `.edit-header` has `padding:12px 24px`, so an 8px vertical expansion on
81:    each side of a 28px control lands at 44px and still sits inside the header's own padding. Nothing
82:    overlaps.
83: 
84: **Why `.dot` is nonetheless carved out, on evidence rather than by inheritance.** Same family (ST
85: editor chrome), different physics, and the fix would make the app worse rather than better:
86: - `.attr-row`/`.skill-row` are `padding:5px 0` with an 18px dot, so the **row pitch is about 29px**.
87:   A 44px vertical hit area would overlap the rows above and below by roughly 7px each. A mis-tap
88:   would then set a *different attribute's* dots. That is a regression, not an improvement.
89: - `.dot-stepper{gap:2px}` gives a **20px horizontal pitch**. A 44px horizontal hit area would overlap
90:   each neighbouring dot by 24px, i.e. every dot's hit area would cover more of its neighbours than of
91:   itself. WCAG 2.5.8's spacing exception exists for exactly this case.
92: - The only real fix is to re-lay-out the editor's Attribute and Skill grids for phone widths, which
93:   is a redesign, is explicitly excluded below, and is constrained by AC3 ("desktop visual design
94:   unchanged") anyway.
95: 
96: So `.dot` goes to carve-out **B3** with its measurements recorded, and the player-facing rating dot
97: the issue was actually describing (`.pref-dot`) is fixed instead.
98: 
99: ## What this story is NOT
100: 
101: - **Not a redesign.** No control changes colour, border, radius, font or label. Where a visual box
102:   does grow (Technique T3 only), it grows **only below 600px** and only where T1 and T2 are proven
103:   unsafe, and each such case is listed by name in the Completion Notes.
104: - **Not a visual-size change on desktop, and not one on phone either, except by the explicit T3
105:   list.** Issue #984's own framing is "pad hit areas (not visual size)". AC3 states the desktop half;
106:   AC4 states the phone half, which the issue leaves implicit. Reinforce both.
107: - **Not gdx-4 (mobile CSS cleanup).** Dead rules, duplicated chrome, selector consolidation, the
108:   inline `style="font-size:Npx"` sites gdx-2 deferred, and the now-dead `.cc-alert.yellow`
109:   declaration all belong to **gdx-4-mobile-css-cleanup**.
110: - **Not gdx-9 (single-scroll sheet).** Sheet relayout is **gdx-9-single-scroll-sheet**, Group C.
111: - **Not a re-do of gdx-2.** `suite.css` and `components.css` are the same two files gdx-2 converted
112:   to `rem`. Do **not** reconvert, do not touch any `font-size`, and do not touch the
113:   `--fs-floor-body` / `--fs-floor-micro` tokens or the player-scoped floor-override block gdx-2
114:   appended to the end of `suite.css`. This story changes box geometry only.
115: - **Not a re-do of CSS-4.** `specs/stories/css-audit/css-4-tap-targets-padding.story.md` (status
116:   `review`) already brought the Territory tracker and several tab containers to 44px. Its results are
117:   live in the tree (`#t-territory button`, `#t-territory .adj`, `#t-territory .back-del` are all at
118:   44px today). Leave them alone.
119: - **Not a tab-container padding pass.** CSS-4's ACs 3 to 5 (outer padding, section spacing) are a
120:   different concern and are not revisited here.
121: - **Not a new breakpoint tier.** Where T3 needs a media query, use the repo's established phone tier
122:   `@media (max-width: 599px)` (`suite.css:88`, `suite.css:2003`) or gdx-2's narrow tier
123:   `@media (max-width: 480px)` (`suite.css:1201`), whichever the measurement actually justifies. Do
124:   not invent a third.
125: - **Not an ARIA or keyboard-accessibility pass.** WCAG 2.5.5 target size only.
126: - **No JS, no HTML, no server, no schema, no MongoDB.** This is a CSS-only story plus a test file.
127:   If a fix appears to need a class added in JS, it is the wrong fix: use a comma-separated selector
128:   list in CSS instead.
129: 
130: ## Carve-outs (deliberate, with reasons)
131: 
132: Each is a real gap, each is recorded, none is silently dropped. Log all three to
133: `specs/deferred-work.md` as part of Task 7. Opening GitHub issues for them is Angelus's call, not
134: the dev agent's.
135: 
136: - **B1 - the Downtime form's own `.dt-` prefixed controls** (roughly 45 selectors from
137:   `components.css:1422` onward, plus `#t-downtime .qf-carthian-remove` at `suite.css:1699`,
138:   `.raw-toggle-btn` at `suite.css:1734`, `.dt-history-summary` at `suite.css:1723` and
139:   `.dt-mobile-show-anyway` at `suite.css:1452`). **Reason: another epic has already ratified a
140:   conflicting target size for this surface.** `specs/epic-dtui-downtime-form-ux-refactor.md`'s NFR9
141:   says "Touch targets >= 32px for tickers and chips; >= 36px for buttons", and
142:   `specs/stories/dtui-2-dt-chip-and-chip-grid.story.md`'s CC6 shipped `min-height:32px` on `.dt-chip`
143:   as a deliberate design decision. `.dt-chip` measures exactly 32px today, i.e. it is *at* its own
144:   ratified floor. Overriding another epic's accepted criterion is a product decision for Angelus, and
145:   the DT form's dense chip grids would re-flow. Note the boundary is the **`.dt-` prefix**, not the
146:   file section: the `.qf-` shared form primitives live in the same section but also render on
147:   Ordeals, Archive, Feeding and the questionnaire, so they stay **in scope**. Raising them to 44px
148:   exceeds DTUI's own ">= 36px for buttons" rather than contradicting it.
149: - **B2 - ST-only surfaces other than the Tracker tab.** `.cbt-*` (Combat tab,
150:   `public/js/game/combat-tab.js`), `#t-territory .regent-sel` (24.4px) and
151:   `#t-territory .peek-toggle-label` (14.4px) - the two stragglers CSS-4 missed - `.stm-*` (ST mods
152:   panel and audit), `.si-*` (Check-In, coordinator-only), `.city-map-*` / `.city-section-hd`,
153:   `.sidebar-st-btn`, and `#desktop-sidebar .sidebar-btn`. **Reason:** the issue's AC1 says
154:   "player-surface controls" and names none of these. The Tracker tab is the one ST-only surface the
