284: ## Dev Notes
285: 
286: ### Existing convention: 44px is already this repo's number, and box growth is already its method
287: 
288: Do not present 44px as a new idea, and check the existing sites before inventing anything:
289: 
290: - `specs/epic-unified-nav.md` NFR2 and UX-DR8: "All interactive tap targets must be >=44px".
291: - `specs/stories/css-audit/css-4-tap-targets-padding.story.md` (status `review`) - Territory tracker
292:   and tab padding. Its results are already in the tree.
293: - `specs/stories/post-game-1/epb-4-sidebar-mobile.story.md`, `.../epc-4-sign-in-tab.story.md`,
294:   `specs/stories/unified-nav/nav-1-2-four-tab-nav.story.md`, `.../nav-1-3b-more-grid-layout.story.md`,
295:   `specs/stories/fin.3.checkin-tab.story.md`.
296: 
297: Live sites that already do it, and are the pattern to match for T1:
298: `components.css:11` (`.char-chip{min-height:44px}`), `components.css:61`
299: (`.exp-row{min-height:44px}`), `components.css:727` (`.sh-stat-icon{width:44px;height:44px}`),
300: `suite.css:378` / `:382` / `:479` (`#t-territory` buttons), `suite.css:485`
301: (`#t-territory .adj{width:44px;height:44px}`), `suite.css:545` (`.feed-reset-btn`), `suite.css:554`
302: (`.feed-adj`), `suite.css:653` (`.trk-dmg-col{min-width:44px}`), `suite.css:1163` (`.si-pay-sel`),
303: `suite.css:1173` (`#roll-char-pools .gcp-pool-chip{min-height:44px}`),
304: `admin-layout.css:150-152`, `admin-spheres.css:48` / `:70`.
305: 
306: **There is no existing hit-area pseudo-element or negative-margin expansion technique in this
307: codebase.** This was checked, not assumed: `public/css/suite.css` and `public/css/components.css`
308: contain **zero** `::after{content:''}` / `::before{content:''}` overlay rules used for hit areas
309: (the only `content:''` in `suite.css` is a decorative badge dot at `:31`), and the only
310: `position:absolute;inset:...` uses are full-bleed overlays and SVG backdrops. So **Technique T2 below
311: is new to this repo** and must be introduced as one documented, commented, reusable block rather than
312: sprinkled per selector.
313: 
314: ### The three techniques, and how to choose
315: 
316: Apply in this order of preference. Measure, then choose; do not choose then measure.
317: 
318: **T1 - direct box growth (`min-height` / `min-width` / `width` / `height`).** The repo's existing
319: convention. Use when the element's box is genuinely invisible, so growing it changes nothing a user
320: sees: no `background`, no `border`, no `box-shadow`, no `border-radius` that shows, **and** no state
321: variant (`.on`, `:hover`, `:focus`, `.filled`) that paints one. Cheapest and most robust. Example:
322: `.pref-dot` has none of those, so T1 is right for it.
323: 
324: **T2 - transparent hit-area pseudo-element.** New to this codebase; introduced by this story. Use
325: when the visual box must not grow (painted background, visible border, segmented control, a tab with
326: an `.on` background). Zero visual change at every width, so it satisfies AC3 and AC4 by construction.
327: 
328: ```css
329: /* gdx-3: hit-area expansion. The visible box is unchanged; the ::after is an
330:    invisible, TAPPABLE overlay centred on it that is never smaller than --tap-min.
331:    Do not add pointer-events:none - that would defeat the entire point. */
332: .sel-a, .sel-b { position: relative; }
333: .sel-a::after, .sel-b::after {
334:   content: '';
335:   position: absolute;
336:   top: 50%;
337:   left: 50%;
338:   transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
339:   width: 100%;
340:   height: 100%;
341:   min-width: var(--tap-min);
342:   min-height: var(--tap-min);
343: }
344: ```
345: 
346: Four traps, all real in this tree:
347: 1. **`overflow:hidden` on an ancestor clips it.** `.svt-toggle` (`suite.css:749`) has
348:    `overflow:hidden`, which is exactly why `.svt-btn` cannot use T2 (Task 5).
349: 2. **`.tab{overflow-x:hidden}` (`suite.css:75`) clips horizontal expansion at the tab edge**, so a
350:    control flush to the left or right edge of a tab gains nothing horizontally. `.tab` is also
351:    `position:absolute;inset:0`, so vertical expansion is fine.
352: 3. **The element must not already have a `::after`.** Grep before adding. If it does, use `::before`,
353:    or T3. Concrete case in this tree: `.rv2-breakdown summary` already declares
354:    `::-webkit-details-marker` (`suite.css:2597`) and `::before` (`suite.css:2598`), so `::after` is
355:    free there but `::before` is not.
356: 4. **The overlay can cover a *sibling* control.** It never steals clicks from its own element (the
357:    handler is on the element), but it will sit over whatever is next to it. This is AC2's whole
358:    point: check the neighbour's geometry before applying.
359: 
360: **T3 - phone-scoped box growth inside a media query.** Use only when T1 and T2 are both unsafe: the
361: box must grow, and the growth is visible. Put it in `@media (max-width: 599px)` (the repo's phone
362: tier, `suite.css:88` and `suite.css:2003`) or gdx-2's `@media (max-width: 480px)`
363: (`suite.css:1201`), whichever the measurement justifies. Desktop is untouched by construction, so
364: AC3 holds; AC4 requires each T3 selector to be named in the Completion Notes. Known T3 cases:
365: `.tbox` (Task 4) and `.svt-btn` (Task 5). Beware specificity, which bit gdx-2: a
366: `body.desktop-mode .x` rule (0,2,0) outranks a plain `.x` inside a media query (0,1,0). Check for a
367: `body.desktop-mode` variant of anything you put in a media query, and match its specificity rather
368: than reaching for `!important`.
369: 
370: ### Viewport emulation gotcha, carried forward from gdx-1 and gdx-2
371: 
372: **`mcp__claude-in-chrome__resize_window` does not actually resize the rendered viewport.** It reports
373: success while `window.innerWidth` stays at the browser's real width, confirmed directly via
374: `javascript_tool` in gdx-1's session. **Do not spend time rediscovering this.** Use one of:
375: - **Playwright's `page.setViewportSize({width:360,height:800})`**, which is real browser-engine
376:   emulation and is already used by several tests in `desktop-and-css.spec.js`. This is the right tool
377:   for touch-target sizing, because it lets you read `getBoundingClientRect()` off the real rendered
378:   DOM at a known width.
379: - Real Chrome DevTools device toolbar (Ctrl+Shift+M) against a locally served build using the
380:   `local-test-token` auth bypass, which is how Angelus completed gdx-1's own sweep.
381: 
382: ### Port 8080 gotcha, also carried forward
383: 
384: An unrelated `python -m http.server 8080` process, not started by the agent session and observed to
385: respawn under a new PID after being stopped, has intermittently shadowed port 8080 and served
386: different content than this project's own `http-server`. It produced a **false-positive green** on
387: gdx-1's regression test. gdx-1 routed around it by serving on 8081. If an assertion passes
388: suspiciously early, check what is actually answering on the port before trusting it.
389: 
390: ### CSS standards apply in full
391: 
392: Per `specs/project-context.md` section 1 and `specs/architecture/coding-standards.md` -> CSS
393: Standards: tokens not literals, no bare hex, no inline `style="..."`, reuse before invent, no
394: `!important`. Use `var(--tap-min)` at every site, never a bare `44px`. Neither
395: `coding-standards.md` nor `project-context.md` currently documents a touch-target convention - the
396: 44px figure lives only in the epic and story files listed above - so consider adding a one-line
397: "Touch targets" entry to `coding-standards.md`'s CSS Standards section pointing at `--tap-min`.
398: That is optional housekeeping, not a task.
399: 
400: ### No database involvement
401: 
402: Pure static-asset story. No server route, no schema, no MongoDB collection, no `tm_suite` write is
403: possible from this change. No data-lock or data-steward check applies.
404: 
405: ### Role and tab map, so "player surface" is not guessed
406: 
407: From `public/js/app.js`'s `NAV_ITEMS` (line 405) and `MORE_APPS` (line ~1900):
408: - **Player tabs:** `dice`, `roll`, `stats`, `skills`, `powers`, `status`, `misc`/`info`, `feeding`,
409:   `downtime`, `ordeals`, `regency`, `office`, `settings`, `archive`, plus `#t-sheets`.
410: - **ST-only (`stOnly:true`):** `territory`, `office-approvals`, `tracker`, `combat`, `spheres`.
411: - **Coordinator-only:** `signin`, `emergency`.
412: - **Reachable inside `index.html` when `getRole()==='st'`:** the full character editor, via
413:   `editorRenderSheet`. This is what puts `.edit-tab` and `.dot` on the page at all.
414: 

