 836:    `document.elementFromPoint` and requires the result to be the element or a descendant. This is
 837:    what actually proves AC1 and AC2 together: `elementFromPoint` respects ancestor clipping (so a
 838:    T2 overlay swallowed by an `overflow:hidden` parent fails even though its computed size says
 839:    44px) and respects paint order (so an overlay covered by a neighbouring control fails too). Edge
 840:    midpoints rather than corners, deliberately, so a rounded corner cannot report a false failure.
 841:    Every one of the eleven selectors moved from T2 to T3 was moved because THIS test caught it.
 842: 4. An AC3 ratchet at 1280px pins the visible box of a representative T1/T2 sample to its authored
 843:    size, so a future "simplification" that swaps an overlay for a `min-height` turns red.
 844: 5. A `.pref-dot` layout test pins the pitch, the first-glyph inset and the row height to their
 845:    pre-gdx-3 values and asserts zero overlap between adjacent hit areas.
 846: 6. A token ratchet asserting `--tap-min` resolves off `:root` to exactly `44px`.
 847: 
 848: Three harness traps were paid for and are written into the comments so the next story does not
 849: repeat them: (a) `app.js` paints the login overlay over everything on an unauthenticated boot, so
 850: the shell has to be revealed first; (b) `app.js:1670` removes whichever of `#t-dice` / `#t-roll` the
 851: `tm-use-new-dice-roller` preference is not using, so one of the two is always absent and has to be
 852: recreated inside the real `.tab-wrap`; (c) **index.html ships `#t-stats` with `class="tab active"`
 853: already on it**, and since every `.tab` is `position:absolute;inset:0`, that one tab silently
 854: swallowed the hit test for every probe mounted in an earlier tab. All `.tab.active` are now parked
 855: and restored around the sweep.
 856: 
 857: **Prove-discriminate (per group, not in aggregate).** Six independent neutralisations, each run with
 858: the rest of the change in place:
